# What Prettier must not touch.
#
# Three categories. Things nobody wrote — dependencies, lockfiles, compiled
# output — things written as prose, where a formatter reflowing a paragraph is a
# worse diff than the one it fixed, and the one document whose formatting IS its
# content.

# --- not written here -------------------------------------------------------

node_modules/
vendor/
build/
tools/
.claude/
package-lock.json
composer.lock
languages/
*.min.js
*.min.css

# --- prose ------------------------------------------------------------------

# README.md and CHANGELOG.md are read on wordpress.org as much as in the repo,
# and docs/ is hand-wrapped so the diffs stay readable. Prettier's markdown
# printer would rewrap every paragraph it touched, which turns a one-word edit
# into a forty-line change.
*.md
readme.txt

# --- not JavaScript ---------------------------------------------------------

# Twig, and PHP-CS-Fixer's business.
*.twig
*.php

# --- laid out on purpose ----------------------------------------------------

# The banner's source, where one <rect> per line IS the drawing: the squares
# read as the grid they render as, the same way the menu mark does in
# class-admin.php. Prettier breaks the long rect across eight lines and joins
# the layered `background` onto one, and the geometry stops being legible at a
# glance — which is the only thing anybody opens this file to check.
assets/src/banner.html
